ilypost.ng/2026/10/16/one-university-many-possibilities-your-future-starts-at-gouni/comments/)", "content_hash": "46853c1afb9c9c6a0936a55e343ff1109cfce7e03f4a3da201c8739310f33b96", "domain": "dailypost", "fetched_at": "2026-10-18T04:29:46Z", "language": "en"}, {"id": "998", "title": "One Home, One Connection: How LG ThinQ Is Making Life Smarter for Nigerians", "url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/one-home-one-connection-how-lg-thinq-is-making-life-smarter-for-nigerians/", "final_url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/one-home-one-connection-how-lg-thinq-is-making-life-smarter-for-nigerians/", "text": "[Sponsored](https://dailypost.ng/sponsored/)One Home, One Connection: How LG ThinQ Is Making Life Smarter for NigeriansPublished on October 16, 2026By [Daily Post Staff](https://dailypost.ng/author/daily-post-staff/)[Comment](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/one-home-one-connection-how-lg-thinq-is-making-life-smarter-for-nigerians/comments/) From cooling the home before you arrive to connecting food care, indoor comfort and entertainment, LG ThinQ puts everyday convenience within reach. What if your home could work more naturally around your day? The air conditioner preparing the room while you are still on your way home. The refrigerator supporting food care in the kitchen. A dehumidifier helping manage indoor humidity. And when the day slows down, the television and audio system turning the living room into a place for football, films and music. This is the idea behind LG ThinQ: bringing compatible LG products together through one connected experience. Through the ThinQ app, users can manage supported LG products from one place, whether at home or away. Depending on the product and model, this can include remote control, monitoring energy use and accessing appliance information. For Nigerian consumers, the value is simple \u2013 less complexity, more convenience, and more time to enjoy life. The Best Technology Knows When to Step InRecommended[Building Genuine connections with people on the internet using the CallMeChat App](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/building-genuine-connections-with-people-on-the-internet-using-the-callmechat-app/)[One university. Many possibilities. Your future starts at GOUNI!](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/one-university-many-possibilities-your-future-starts-at-gouni/)[Global expectations soar as Healing Streams returns for final 2026 edition](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/15/global-expectations-soar-as-healing-streams-returns-for-final-2026-edition/) Good technology should not constantly ask for attention. Sometimes, it should simply be there when you need it. When hunger calls, the refrigerator and NeoChef microwave have a role to play. When Nigerian heat follows you all the way home, the AC matters. When humidity becomes part of the indoor environment, the dehumidifier has its moment. And when the working day is finally over, LG TV and audio can turn the same home into a front-row seat for football, a cinema for the family or the soundtrack to an evening with friends. LG ThinQ provides the connection across compatible LG products, giving consumers one place to interact with their connected home. The result is not technology competing for attention in every room. It is technology showing up at the right moments. Because sometimes intelligent living is as simple as arriving home to greater comfort, finding dinner easier to manage, or pressing play and spending the rest of the evening with the people who matter. \u201cAt LG, we believe technology should work around people, not the other way around,\u201d said Hyoung Sub Ji, Managing Director, LG Electronics West Africa. \u201cWith LG ThinQ, our goal is to bring compatible products together in a way that makes everyday living more convenient and intuitive. From the kitchen to home comfort and entertainment, innovation becomes meaningful when consumers can feel the difference it makes in their lives.\u201d Connected by Innovation, Strengthened by Trust This vision comes at a significant moment in LG Electronics\u2019 relationship with Nigerian consumers as the brand was named Most Trusted Electronic Brand in Nigeria at the fifth Consumer Value Awards, securing 57.1 per cent of the consumer and citizen voice vote in the television category. That recognition matters because the award was determined through consumer and citizen voting. Trust, after all, is particularly important when technology becomes part of the everyday rhythm of the home. As Paul Mba, Head of Corporate Marketing, LG Electronics Nigeria, said following the recognition: \u201cBeing recognised as the Most Trusted Electronic Brand is a meaningful reflection of the confidence consumers place in LG. For us, trust is built every day through innovation that genuinely improves lives, quality products and a commitment to delivering experiences that put consumers first.\u201d One Brand. One Home. One Intelligent Life. There is no single definition of a perfect Nigerian home, but there are familiar moments. Breakfast before the rush. Coming home after a demanding day. Finding relief from the heat. Keeping the home comfortable during humid weather. Friends arriving for football. Music on a Saturday evening. Movie night with the family. The TV, Audio, Washing Machine, Refrigerator, Microwave, Air Conditioner and Dehumidifier each have a different role, LG ThinQ provides the connected layer brings compatibility to all LG products into one easier-to-manage experience. Because the smartest home should not necessarily be the home with the most technology. It should be the home where technology makes everyday life feel easier. To know more about LG ThinQ, visit [https://www.lg.com/africa/lg-thinq](https://www.lg.com/africa/lg-thinq)Share this story[WhatsApp](https://wa.me/?text=One%20Home%2C%20One%20Connection%3A%20How%20LG%20ThinQ%20Is%20Making%20Life%20Smarter%20for%20Nigerians%20https%3A%2F%2Fdailypost.ng%2F2026%2F10%2F16%2Fone-home-one-connection-how-lg-thinq-is-making-life-smarter-for-nigerians%2F) Facebook You may like[Stockity: Digital Trading Platforms Gain Ground as More Users Explore Financial Markets Online](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/15/stockity-digital-trading-platforms-gain-ground-as-more-users-explore-financial-markets-online/)[OPay named Digital Bank and Financial Inclusion Leader at BAFI 2026](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/15/opay-named-digital-bank-and-financial-inclusion-leader-at-bafi-2026/)[Renewed Hope Cities: Tinubu\u2019s Housing Initiative draws over 100,000 Nigerians as projects expand nationwide](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/15/renewed-hope-cities-tinubus-housing-initiative-draws-over-100000-nigerians-as-projects-expand-nationwide-3/)[Join the conversation](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/one-home-one-connection-how-lg-thinq-is-making-life-smarter-for-nigerians/comments/)", "content_hash": "d768336a2d5d5041d98341d81ddea036d40098d1505364b08d83c72eab1fafd4", "domain": "dailypost", "fetched_at": "2026-10-18T04:29:47Z", "language": "en"}, {"id": "999", "title": "Global expectations soar as Healing Streams returns for final 2026 edition", "url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/15/global-expectations-soar-as-healing-streams-returns-for-final-2026-edition/", "final_url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/15/global-expectations-soar-as-healing-streams-returns-for-final-2026-edition/", "text": "[Sponsored](https://dailypost.ng/sponsored/)Global expectations soar as Healing Streams returns for final 2026 editionPublished on October 15, 2026By [Daily Post Staff](https://dailypost.ng/author/daily-post-staff/)[Comment](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/15/global-expectations-soar-as-healing-streams-returns-for-final-2026-edition/comments/) The Healing Streams Live Healing Services with Pastor Chris Oyakhilome will return from October 23 to 25, 2026, at 2 pm (GMT+1) daily, with expectations rising for another global event centred on faith, prayer and healing. Building on previous editions, the three-day event is expected to attract participants from different countries, with organisers anticipating testimonies of healing and personal transformation. The final edition of 2026 is expected to draw participants seeking to experience what they describe as the love, mercy and healing power of God. An open invitation to the worldRecommended[Building Genuine connections with people on the internet using the CallMeChat App](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/building-genuine-connections-with-people-on-the-internet-using-the-callmechat-app/)[One university. Many possibilities. Your future starts at GOUNI!](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/one-university-many-possibilities-your-future-starts-at-gouni/)[One Home, One Connection: How LG ThinQ Is Making Life Smarter for Nigerians](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/one-home-one-connection-how-lg-thinq-is-making-life-smarter-for-nigerians/) Registration is free and open to people worldwide at healingstreams.org. Registrants are encouraged to indicate whether they or their loved ones need healing so they can receive guidance and access preparatory faith classes and materials. The invitation extends beyond those seeking physical healing. Pastor Chris Oyakhilome, convener of the event, has repeatedly emphasised the importance of God\u2019s Word, describing the programme as an opportunity for people of all ages and circumstances to encounter the message of Christ, strengthen their faith and experience God\u2019s presence. One message, every language, every nation As in previous editions, the event will be streamed live and translated into multiple languages and major dialects, bringing together participants from diverse cultural backgrounds. According to the organisers, millions of Healing Centres have been established in towns, villages, hospitals, prisons, orphanages, homes and other locations worldwide to enable individuals, families and groups to participate. \u2018We can change their world\u2019 \u2014 Pastor Chris calls for global participation Ahead of the event, Pastor Chris Oyakhilome has called for a global mobilisation to ensure that more people can participate in the programme. Speaking recently during the Global Communion Service, he said: \u201cIt\u2019s just a few more days; we will have the Healing Streams Live Healing Services, and it is going to be huge. By the power of the Holy Spirit, the healing graces of God, the Angels of God, will cover this world, and many will be healed; especially in this month of mercies.\u201d He highlighted the programme\u2019s importance to people seeking relief from illnesses and urged ministers of the Gospel worldwide to work together to expand its reach. \u201cWe have to mobilize all that the Lord has given us authority to control and to influence. Get everyone ready for Healing Streams. We can change their world.\u201d Referring to testimonies from previous editions, Pastor Chris said the programme could bring blessings to people of all ages. \u201cThis is something that will bring so much blessing to old and young alike. Think about babies, children who have never walked because of some debilitating disease. And during the Healing Streams, they will begin to walk. The deaf will hear, the dumb will speak, the blind will see; God\u2019s going to change their world completely because of the Healing Streams. Even the dead will be raised,\u201d he said. He urged people to prepare for the event, expressing his belief that it would provide an opportunity for people worldwide to experience God\u2019s glory. \u201cI want you to look forward to Healing Streams, prepare for it, plan for it; because the glory of God will be made manifest around the world,\u201d he added. A legacy of testimonies According to the organisers, previous editions of the programme have generated numerous testimonies of reported healings and personal transformations, including accounts involving people who had experienced serious health conditions. The organisers say these testimonies, shared by participants from different countries and backgrounds, have continued to generate interest in subsequent editions of the Healing Streams Live Healing Services. Expectations rise across nations With the October edition approaching, participants from different countries have expressed their expectations for the programme. Sakshi Telure from India said she was looking forward to the event and encouraged others to share information about it with their friends and families. \u201cI\u2019m filled with expectation for this edition of the Healing Streams Live Healing Services. I believe even more amazing things are going to happen this time, and I\u2019m excited to share the news with everyone I know. \u201cI encourage you to share it with your friends and family because I believe that, whether you need healing, restoration, or a breakthrough in any area of your life, you can receive your miracle. I\u2019m so excited and full of expectation for what God is going to do. I believe many people will experience the Lord\u2019s grace, mercy, and love through the Healing Streams Live Healing Services. Praise the Lord!\u201d she said. Shabib from Nigeria said he was hoping for improvements in his health and finances. \u201cI\u2019m expecting a miracle in my health and finances in this edition. I believe the pain I have suffered for many years due to a spinal injury will finally leave me permanently, along with the high blood pressure and weakness that have plagued me. My faith is high, and my expectation shall not be cut off,\u201d he said. Vanessa from Canada said she hoped the event would reach people who had lost hope, particularly in her country. \u201cI\u2019m expecting this Healing Streams to reach people who may have lost hope and their way, especially in my country. I believe many will encounter the healing power of God and experience miracles they never thought possible, and, most importantly, receive salvation,\u201d she said. Steve from Germany also expressed optimism about the forthcoming edition. \u201cI expect that this edition will surpass everything we have witnessed before. I\u2019m looking forward to countless testimonies of healing, restoration, and salvation from people across the nations,\u201d he said. Global mobilisation intensifies Organisers say preparations for the event are intensifying, with individuals and groups mobilising participants in communities around the world. Activities include establishing Healing Centres, distributing Healing to the Nations magazines and participating in a 24-hour prayer chain, through which Christians are praying for the sick and those expected to participate in the programme. The mobilisation is aimed at expanding awareness of the event and encouraging more people to take part in the final edition of the year. Road to Healing Streams returns with season 18 As part of the preparations, Road to Healing Streams Live Healing Services returns with its 18th season, featuring reports on preparations, testimonies and faith-based activities taking place ahead of the event. The programme airs daily on Healing Streams TV at 12 noon and 4 pm (GMT+1) until Thursday, October 22. It features activities by ministries, churches, organisations, volunteers and individuals preparing their communities through healing crusades, evangelism campaigns, prayer initiatives, Healing Centre mobilisation and community outreach programmes. The broadcast also features testimonies from participants who attribute reported improvements in their conditions to their involvement in previous editions of the programme. Reported healing testimonies from the July edition Jos\u00e9 Mar\u00edn \u2014 Panama According to the organisers, Jos\u00e9 Mar\u00edn had experienced severe pain and limited mobility in his leg and spine for two years following an accident. He reportedly experienced relief during the July edition of the Healing Streams Live Healing Services after Pastor Chris prayed for participants seeking healing. The organisers said Mar\u00edn subsequently reported that the pain had disappeared and his mobility had improved. Cheany\u2019s son \u2014 Vietnam The organisers said Cheany\u2019s son had spent 28 days on a ventilator after his right lung collapsed. According to the account, Cheany participated in the programme from her son\u2019s hospital bedside and laid hands on him while Pastor Chris prayed. She subsequently reported an improvement in her son\u2019s condition. Vanessa \u2014 Canada Vanessa reportedly lived with type 2 diabetes for five years and experienced neuropathy, vision problems, pain and swelling in her feet. Following her participation in the July edition, she reported that the burning sensation, tingling and swelling had disappeared and that she could walk, sit and stand more comfortably. Pauline Atu \u2014 Nigeria Pauline Atu from Cross River State reportedly suffered from arthritis for a year, making walking, running, jumping, sitting and sleeping difficult because of pain. According to the organisers, she experienced an improvement during the Healing Streams programme and subsequently reported being able to walk, run and jump freely. Adiel \u2014 Ecuador Five-year-old Adiel reportedly had difficulty speaking from birth. According to the organisers, his mother brought him to a Healing Streams centre in the hope that he would receive healing. During the programme, he reportedly began speaking more clearly and subsequently communicated more fluently. The accounts above are testimonies reported by participants or organisers and have not been independently medically verified. How to participate The Healing Streams Live Healing Services will hold from October 23 to 25, 2026, with daily sessions beginning at 2 pm (GMT+1). The organisers said the services would be streamed on Healing Streams TV, LoveWorld Networks and selected terrestrial television and radio stations worldwide. Registration is free through the programme\u2019s website. Media contact: Healing Streams Communications Email: [[email protected]](https://dailypost.ng/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#177e797178577f72767b7e797064636572767a64396361) Phone numbers: South Africa: +27 799 675 852 Nigeria: +234 (1) 888 5066 USA: +1 832 724 9390 Canada: +1 289 622 1634 UK: +44 (0) 333 188 0710 Asia: +91 96500 96633 India: +91 77949 93762 Website: healingstreams.tvShare this story[WhatsApp](https://wa.me/?text=Global%20expectations%20soar%20as%20Healing%20Streams%20returns%20for%20final%202026%20edition%20https%3A%2F%2Fdailypost.ng%2F2026%2F10%2F15%2Fglobal-expectations-soar-as-healing-streams-returns-for-final-2026-edition%2F) Facebook You may like[Stockity: Digital Trading Platforms Gain Ground as More Users Explore Financial Markets Online](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/15/stockity-digital-trading-platforms-gain-ground-as-more-users-explore-financial-markets-online/)[OPay named Digital Bank and Financial Inclusion Leader at BAFI 2026](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/15/opay-named-digital-bank-and-financial-inclusion-leader-at-bafi-2026/)[Renewed Hope Cities: Tinubu\u2019s Housing Initiative draws over 100,000 Nigerians as projects expand nationwide](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/15/renewed-hope-cities-tinubus-housing-initiative-draws-over-100000-nigerians-as-projects-expand-nationwide-3/)[Join the conversation](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/15/global-expectations-soar-as-healing-streams-returns-for-final-2026-edition/comments/)", "content_hash": "9712adb13fee6ba77e67e57fa65910ee3d0bb47a434e09e28020c518017c43ac", "domain": "dailypost", "fetched_at": "2026-10-18T04:29:49Z", "language": "en"}, {"id": "1000", "title": "2027: NDC candidate raises alarm over alleged plot to remove party from ballot in Lagos", "url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/2027-ndc-candidate-raises-alarm-over-alleged-plot-to-remove-party-from-ballot-in-lagos-2/", "final_url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/2027-ndc-candidate-raises-alarm-over-alleged-plot-to-remove-party-from-ballot-in-lagos-2/", "text": "[Politics](https://dailypost.ng/politics/)2027: NDC candidate raises alarm over alleged plot to remove party from ballot in Lagos Published on October 17, 2026By [Ochogwu Sunday](https://dailypost.ng/author/ochogwu-sunday/)[Comment](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/2027-ndc-candidate-raises-alarm-over-alleged-plot-to-remove-party-from-ballot-in-lagos-2/comments/)The Nigeria Democratic Congress (NDC) House of Representatives candidate for Surulere I Federal Constituency, Lagos State, Adefolaseye Adebayo, has alleged a plot by the ruling All Progressives Congress (APC) to prevent the party from appearing on the ballot in the 2027 general elections.Adebayo, who is also the South-West Coordinator of the OK Movement, made the allegation in a video shared on her official X handle on Saturday.She claimed to have received information that some individuals were planning to ensure that the NDC would not appear on the ballot for the Surulere I Federal Constituency.\u201cI got information that some group of people are planning to make sure that NDC does not appear on the ballot for the Surulere I Federal Constituency.Recommended[2027: No vacancy in Aso Rock, North will vote 100 per cent for Tinubu - Kano Gov, Yusuf](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/2027-no-vacancy-in-aso-rock-north-will-vote-100-for-tinubu-kano-gov-yusuf-2/)[2027: G-100 coalition reveals when opposition will pick single candidate to face Tinubu](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/2027-g-100-coalition-reveals-when-opposition-will-pick-single-candidate-to-face-tinubu/)[2027: Tinubu an absentee President not fit for re-election - Kenneth Okonkwo](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/tinubu-cannot-meet-nigerians-directly-kenneth-okonkwo/)\u201cI'm calling on the INEC chairman to take note,\u201d she said.Adebayo further alleged that a similar incident occurred during the 2023 general elections, when the Labour Party was allegedly removed from the ballot.\u201cThey did it during the last federal election for the House of Representatives in Surulere I with the Labour Party, when the person who was the Labour Party candidate colluded with them, and the Labour Party did not appear on the ballot paper.\u201cNothing happened because the candidate was part of the game plan. They got away with it then, and now they want to repeat it again,\u201d she said.She further called on the party's leadership and Nigerians to take note of the alleged plot, urging them to ensure that such a situation was not allowed to recur.Share this story[WhatsApp](https://wa.me/?text=2027%3A%20NDC%20candidate%20raises%20alarm%20over%20alleged%20plot%20to%20remove%20party%20from%20ballot%20in%20Lagos%20%20https%3A%2F%2Fdailypost.ng%2F2026%2F10%2F17%2F2027-ndc-candidate-raises-alarm-over-alleged-plot-to-remove-party-from-ballot-in-lagos-2%2F) FacebookYou may like[2027: ADC faction disowns Atiku, rejects alliance with G-100](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/atiku-under-pressure-as-adc-faction-rejects-alliance-with-g-100/)[2027 elections: Kano police warn against fake news, boast of robust security](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/2027-elections-kano-police-warn-against-fake-news-assure-robust-security/)[2027: Atiku, Peter Obi, Adebayo, others to state position on opposition coalition against Tinubu \u2013 Lukman](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/2027-atiku-peter-obi-adebayo-others-to-make-public-statements-on-opposition-coalition-against-unseat-tinubu-lukman/)[Join the conversation](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/2027-ndc-candidate-raises-alarm-over-alleged-plot-to-remove-party-from-ballot-in-lagos-2/comments/)", "content_hash": "0bf16f18fe3774e52f0b68453432e0c18241dd5382b5b3efe52bd10ce9e8c0a5", "domain": "dailypost", "fetched_at": "2026-10-18T04:29:50Z", "language": "en"}, {"id": "1001", "title": "2027: Tinubu an absentee President not fit for re-election - Kenneth Okonkwo", "url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/tinubu-cannot-meet-nigerians-directly-kenneth-okonkwo/", "final_url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/tinubu-canno