ingos/comments/) Poland U-17 women\u2019s head coach, Paulina Kawalec is targeting a positive start against Nigeria\u2019s Flamingos at the 2026 FIFA U-17 Women\u2019s World Cup. The Poles will open their campaign at the tournament against Akeem Busari\u2019s side at the Mohammed V1 Football Complex Pitch 4, Rabat on Saturday (today). The Europeans will also face defending DPR Korea, and Puerto Rico in Group B. Kawalec said it is important for his team to start the competition on a winning note.Recommended[EPL: Iwobi's goal earns Fulham first win of season](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/epl-iwobis-goal-earns-fulham-first-win-of-season/)[Turkey: Two top players Galatasaray want to sign in January transfer window revealed](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/turkey-two-top-players-galatasaray-want-to-sign-in-january-transfer-window-revealed/)[LaLiga: I don't want new players at Real Madrid - Mourinho](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/laliga-i-dont-want-new-players-at-real-madrid-mourinho/) \u201cOpening games at big tournaments are always of huge importance. In our group, the game against Nigeria could be particularly important and have a major influence on how the rest of the tournament unfolds,\u201d Kawalec told FIFA. The encounter will kick-off at 7pm Nigeria time.Share this story[WhatsApp](https://wa.me/?text=2026%20U-17%20WWC%3A%20Poland%20coach%C2%A0eyes%20winning%20start%20against%20Flamingos%20https%3A%2F%2Fdailypost.ng%2F2026%2F10%2F17%2F2026-u-17-wwc-poland-coach-eyes-winning-start-against-flamingos%2F) Facebook You may like[NPFL: Abdallah upbeat Ranchers Bees will recover from poor start](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/npfl-abdallah-upbeat-ranchers-bees-will-recover-from-poor-start/)[LaLiga: I would have left Real Madrid if I was Vinicius Jr \u2013 Mourinho](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/laliga-i-would-have-left-real-madrid-if-i-was-vinicius-jr-mourinho/)[EPL: Unbeaten Everton chase statement win vs Chelsea as Moyes plots revenge against Alonso](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/epl-unbeaten-everton-chase-statement-win-vs-chelsea-as-moyes-plots-revenge-against-alonso/)[Join the conversation](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/2026-u-17-wwc-poland-coach-eyes-winning-start-against-flamingos/comments/)", "content_hash": "c2acc0ad209266484f8d865f96779ff2e6a00055d5e3578a3d4f5af0e93d438f", "domain": "dailypost", "fetched_at": "2026-10-18T04:29:58Z", "language": "en"}, {"id": "1007", "title": "UBA wins N156bn debt recovery suit against Stallion Group, Vaswani Brothers", "url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/uba-wins-n156bn-debt-recovery-suit-against-stallion-group-vaswani-brothers/", "final_url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/uba-wins-n156bn-debt-recovery-suit-against-stallion-group-vaswani-brothers/", "text": "[Business](https://dailypost.ng/business/)UBA wins N156bn debt recovery suit against Stallion Group, Vaswani BrothersPublished on October 17, 2026By [Ogaga Ariemu](https://dailypost.ng/author/ogaga-ariemu/)[Comment](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/uba-wins-n156bn-debt-recovery-suit-against-stallion-group-vaswani-brothers/comments/)United Bank for Africa, UBA, Plc has secured a court ruling in its three-year effort to recover funds it says Stallion Group owes. The Federal High Court upheld the bank\u2019s receiver-manager appointment, its mortgage security and the liability of the guarantors.Justice Daniel Osiagor of the Federal High Court in Ikoyi, Lagos, resolved all issues in UBA\u2019s favour and granted all the reliefs sought, according to a report by MoneyCentral on the judgment delivered by the court.The court confirmed Romeo Ese Michael as receiver-manager, with the authority to take possession of the mortgaged property and seek protective orders.Recommended[FG commissions 1MW Solar Mini-Grid, begins construction of 16MW projects in Gombe](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/fg-commissions-1mw-solar-mini-grid-begins-construction-of-16mw-projects-in-gombe/)[Dollar-to-Naira exchange rate Today, October 16, 2026: Naira depreciates against USD to end week on negative note](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/dollar-to-naira-exchange-rate-today-october-16-2026-naira-depreciates-against-usd-to-end-week-on-negative-note/)[Food Inflation: Three Nigerian states with slowest price hikes in September](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/food-inflation-three-nigerian-states-with-slowest-price-hikes-in-september/)It also restrained the defendants from diverting payments owed to them by government agencies, thereby reinforcing the bank\u2019s ability to protect its recovery interests.The court held that the defendants did not dispute their indebtedness but contested the amount owed. It further ruled that the reconciliation of accounts did not extinguish the debt.The court also dismissed objections raised by the 12th defendant, Barbedos Ventures Limited, holding that it had failed to establish any proprietary rights over the mortgaged property. Consequently, its consent was not required for the creation of the mortgage, and its objections were rejected.When UBA filed the suit in October 2023, it claimed that \u20a6156.03 billion was owed to the bank. Stallion Group has described the claim as \u201centirely false\". However, the court\u2019s written judgment and Stallion Group\u2019s response to the ruling were not immediately available.The case began when Justice Akintayo Aluko granted UBA orders to take over the assets of Stallion Nigeria Ltd. and its affiliates in Lagos, Port Harcourt and Kano, and to freeze their funds across Nigerian banks. The defendants\u2019 attempts to lift the orders failed in December 2023.The defendants include Von Automobile Nigeria, Stallion Motors, The Honda Place and director Sunil Vaswani.The ruling reinforces a principle Nigerian lenders rely on: disputing the amount owed does not, in itself, prevent a creditor from enforcing its security. UBA is using the same receiver-manager to pursue N61.45 billion linked to Western Metal Products Co.The decision represents a significant victory for UBA, with the court resolving all issues in the bank\u2019s favour and granting the reliefs sought.The ruling is particularly significant for the enforcement of creditors\u2019 rights in Nigeria, underscoring the legal validity of properly constituted security arrangements and the authority of duly appointed receivers to protect and enforce creditors\u2019 interests.The judgment marks a major milestone in UBA\u2019s efforts to recover its exposure to Stallion Group and safeguard the interests of the bank and its stakeholders.Key highlights of the judgmentThe Federal High Court in Ikoyi affirmed its jurisdiction to hear the case.The judgment was delivered by Justice Daniel Osiagor of Court 6 of the Federal High Court, Ikoyi, Lagos.The defendants did not dispute their indebtedness but contested the amount owed.The guarantors were held liable.The appointment of the receiver-manager was upheld as valid.The receiver-manager\u2019s right to take possession of the mortgaged property was affirmed.The receiver-manager was held entitled to seek protective orders.The court held that the reconciliation exercise did not extinguish the indebtedness.The objection raised by the 12th defendant was dismissed because it failed to establish any proprietary rights over the mortgaged property. Its consent was therefore not required for the mortgage.The defendants were restrained from diverting receivables due to them from government agencies.Share this story[WhatsApp](https://wa.me/?text=UBA%20wins%20N156bn%20debt%20recovery%20suit%20against%20Stallion%20Group%2C%20Vaswani%20Brothers%20https%3A%2F%2Fdailypost.ng%2F2026%2F10%2F17%2Fuba-wins-n156bn-debt-recovery-suit-against-stallion-group-vaswani-brothers%2F) FacebookYou may like[Inflation: Three Nigerian states with highest food price hikes in September 2026](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/inflation-three-nigerian-states-with-highest-food-price-hikes-in-september-2026/)[IMF chief urges countries to develop policies embedded in AI](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/imf-chief-urges-countries-to-develop-policies-embedded-in-ai/)[Taraba farmers may stop irrigation farming over fuel price surge](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/taraba-farmers-may-stop-irrigation-farming-over-fuel-price-surge/)[Join the conversation](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/uba-wins-n156bn-debt-recovery-suit-against-stallion-group-vaswani-brothers/comments/)", "content_hash": "aeb4079fd6dcf725d2aa71ddadba7e63a01fe0120467e17bf3414a62705ff497", "domain": "dailypost", "fetched_at": "2026-10-18T04:30:01Z", "language": "en"}, {"id": "1008", "title": "FG commissions 1MW Solar Mini-Grid, begins construction of 16MW projects in Gombe", "url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/fg-commissions-1mw-solar-mini-grid-begins-construction-of-16mw-projects-in-gombe/", "final_url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/fg-commissions-1mw-solar-mini-grid-begins-construction-of-16mw-projects-in-gombe/", "text": "[Business](https://dailypost.ng/business/)FG commissions 1MW Solar Mini-Grid, begins construction of 16MW projects in GombePublished on October 17, 2026By [Ogaga Ariemu](https://dailypost.ng/author/ogaga-ariemu/)[Comment](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/fg-commissions-1mw-solar-mini-grid-begins-construction-of-16mw-projects-in-gombe/comments/)The Federal Government has commissioned a 1-megawatt, MW, solar mini-grid project equipped with a 2.4-megawatt-hour, MWh battery energy storage system, in Tallasse community of Balanga Local Government Area, Gombe State.The commissioning ceremony, held on Saturday, also marked the official groundbreaking for four additional interconnected mini-grid projects with a combined capacity of 16MW across Dukku, Bajoga, Kumo and Kaltungo communities in Gombe State.The project also features the deployment and launch of productive-use equipment, including electric tricycles, an electric groundnut oil processing plant, a modular electric rice mill and electric multi-flour grinding machines. The equipment is designed to connect reliable electricity directly to mobility, agriculture, processing, enterprise and income generation.This follows the recent groundbreaking ceremony for a 17.7MW interconnected mini-grid project in Iwo, Ibadan, Oyo State, on Wednesday.Recommended[Phone traders urge FG, NCC to suspend registration fees for 90 days](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/phone-traders-warn-of-job-losses-demand-90-day-suspension-of-phone-registration-fees/)[Nigerian youths ready to play role in national development - Niger Delta activist to FG](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/being-youth-shouldnt-be-disqualification-for-national-assignment-niger-delta-activist-to-fg/)[UBA wins N156bn debt recovery suit against Stallion Group, Vaswani Brothers](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/uba-wins-n156bn-debt-recovery-suit-against-stallion-group-vaswani-brothers/)Speaking at the commissioning ceremony, the Governor of Gombe State, Muhammadu Inuwa Yahaya, described the project as another important outcome of the strategic partnership between the Gombe State Government and the Federal Government through the Rural Electrification Agency, REA.\u201cFor us in Gombe State, this project is significant because it connects energy directly to the economic strengths of our people. Balanga is an agricultural community. When reliable electricity is combined with rice milling, groundnut processing, flour production and electric mobility, we are not merely lighting homes; we are strengthening an entire local economy.\u201cOur partnership with the Rural Electrification Agency demonstrates what can be achieved when federal and state governments align around a common development objective. We deeply appreciate His Excellency, President Bola Ahmed Tinubu, the Honourable Minister of Power and the leadership of REA for translating policy into infrastructure that our people can see, use and benefit from. This is Renewed Hope made tangible at the community level,\u201d the governor said.In his remarks, the Minister of Power, Joseph Tegbe, emphasised that the projects reflects the practical realisation of President Bola Tinubu\u2019s Renewed Hope Agenda, which seeks to ensure that citizens\u2019 access to opportunities is not determined by their geographical location.\u201cFrom Kwara State and the Federal Capital Territory to last Wednesday\u2019s event in Oyo State, and now here in Gombe, renewable power is spreading across Nigeria with unmistakable momentum.\u201cThis is the practical expression of President Bola Ahmed Tinubu\u2019s Renewed Hope Agenda: taking investment to communities and expanding the foundations of shared prosperity,\u201d Tegbe stated.The minister noted that the true value of the infrastructure extends beyond basic household lighting, with the projects aimed at promoting rural economic empowerment.\u201cThe true significance of these investments will be measured in the daily lives they improve: the farmer who can process produce closer to home, the trader who can preserve perishable goods, the artisan who can power equipment, and the young person who can build a livelihood within the community,\u201d Tegbe added.Also speaking, the Managing Director and Chief Executive Officer of the Rural Electrification Agency, Abba Aliyu, said the 1MW project directly serves 6,028 connections, comprising 5,929 residential units, 84 commercial connections and 15 dedicated nodes for productive economic activities.He noted that Balanga represents the direction in which REA is taking rural electrification nationwide, shifting the focus from simply counting connections to measuring the economic outcomes enabled by electricity.\u201cFor many years, the conversation around electricity access has understandably focused on how many people we connect and how many megawatts we deploy. Those numbers remain important. But the next frontier is to ask a more fundamental question: what happens after the electricity arrives?\u201cDoes the farmer process more of what he produces? Does a young entrepreneur establish a new business? Does the cost of mobility reduce? Can a woman who previously spent hours processing agricultural produce increase her productivity and income? Can businesses operate longer and employ more people? Those are the outcomes that ultimately define successful electrification,\u201d Aliyu said.He added that the inclusion of a 2.4MWh battery energy storage system also demonstrates REA\u2019s growing emphasis on the reliability and quality of electricity supply.\u201cAccess without reliability limits economic impact. This is why we are increasingly integrating storage, intelligent monitoring, productive-use equipment and sustainable operating models into our interventions. We are building electricity ecosystems, not simply installing power plants,\u201d he said.Share this story[WhatsApp](https://wa.me/?text=FG%20commissions%201MW%20Solar%20Mini-Grid%2C%20begins%20construction%20of%2016MW%20projects%20in%20Gombe%20https%3A%2F%2Fdailypost.ng%2F2026%2F10%2F17%2Ffg-commissions-1mw-solar-mini-grid-begins-construction-of-16mw-projects-in-gombe%2F) FacebookYou may like[Dollar-to-Naira exchange rate Today, October 16, 2026: Naira depreciates against USD to end week on negative note](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/dollar-to-naira-exchange-rate-today-october-16-2026-naira-depreciates-against-usd-to-end-week-on-negative-note/)[FG laments effect of poor communication network in hinterlands](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/fg-laments-effect-of-poor-communication-network-in-hinterlands/)[Food Inflation: Three Nigerian states with slowest price hikes in September](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/food-inflation-three-nigerian-states-with-slowest-price-hikes-in-september/)[Join the conversation](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/fg-commissions-1mw-solar-mini-grid-begins-construction-of-16mw-projects-in-gombe/comments/)", "content_hash": "623dd2da1a8ba2e7de031d8d6e400b1f9c1908b255001746591b192feaf34d7b", "domain": "dailypost", "fetched_at": "2026-10-18T04:30:02Z", "language": "en"}, {"id": "1009", "title": "Dollar-to-Naira exchange rate Today, October 16, 2026: Naira depreciates against USD to end week on negative note", "url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/dollar-to-naira-exchange-rate-today-october-16-2026-naira-depreciates-against-usd-to-end-week-on-negative-note/", "final_url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/dollar-to-naira-exchange-rate-today-october-16-2026-naira-depreciates-against-usd-to-end-week-on-negative-note/", "text": "[Business](https://dailypost.ng/business/)Dollar-to-Naira exchange rate Today, October 16, 2026: Naira depreciates against USD to end week on negative notePublished on October 16, 2026By [Ogaga Ariemu](https://dailypost.ng/author/ogaga-ariemu/)[Comment](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/dollar-to-naira-exchange-rate-today-october-16-2026-naira-depreciates-against-usd-to-end-week-on-negative-note/comments/) The naira depreciated against the United States dollar at the official foreign exchange market on Friday. Central Bank of Nigeria, CBN, data showed that the naira weakened to \u20a61,332.26 per dollar on Friday, from \u20a61,331.61 recorded on Thursday. This means that, on a day-to-day basis, the naira depreciated by \u20a60.65 against the dollar. However, on a week-on-week basis, the naira gained \u20a61.07 against the dollar at the official foreign exchange market.Recommended[UBA wins N156bn debt recovery suit against Stallion Group, Vaswani Brothers](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/uba-wins-n156bn-debt-recovery-suit-against-stallion-group-vaswani-brothers/)[FG commissions 1MW Solar Mini-Grid, begins construction of 16MW projects in Gombe](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/fg-commissions-1mw-solar-mini-grid-begins-construction-of-16mw-projects-in-gombe/)[Food Inflation: Three Nigerian states with slowest price hikes in September](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/food-inflation-three-nigerian-states-with-slowest-price-hikes-in-september/) DAILY POST reports that the naira appreciated to \u20a61,370 per dollar at the parallel market on Friday, after remaining stable at \u20a61,375 per dollar since Monday. The development comes as the country\u2019s external reserves stood at $55.09 billion, according to CBN data. DAILY POST reports that the naira recorded mixed performance against the dollar during the week under review.Share this story[WhatsApp](https://wa.me/?text=Dollar-to-Naira%20exchange%20rate%20Today%2C%20October%2016%2C%202026%3A%20Naira%20depreciates%20against%20USD%20to%20end%20week%20on%20negative%20note%20https%3A%2F%2Fdailypost.ng%2F2026%2F10%2F16%2Fdollar-to-naira-exchange-rate-today-october-16-2026-naira-depreciates-against-usd-to-end-week-on-negative-note%2F) Facebook [Dollar-to-Naira exchange rate Today, October 15, 2026: Naira extends appreciation against USD](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/15/dollar-to-naira-exchange-rate-today-october-15-2026-naira-extends-appreciation-against-usd/) You may like[Inflation: Three Nigerian states with highest food price hikes in September 2026](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/inflation-three-nigerian-states-with-highest-food-price-hikes-in-september-2026/)[IMF chief urges countries to develop policies embedded in AI](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/imf-chief-urges-countries-to-develop-policies-embedded-in-ai/)[Taraba farmers may stop irrigation farming over fuel price surge](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/taraba-farmers-may-stop-irrigation-farming-over-fuel-price-surge/)[Join the conversation](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/dollar-to-naira-exchange-rate-today-october-16-2026-naira-depreciates-against-usd-to-end-week-on-negative-note/comments/)", "content_hash": "50df8af22b3e2f5713f6def1719d15e32ac7d21ef8cb149c7cca9166c6d8bcce", "domain": "dailypost", "fetched_at": "2026-10-18T04:30:04Z", "language": "en"}, {"id": "1010", "title": "Food Inflation: Three Nigerian states with slowest price hikes in September", "url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/food-inflation-three-nigerian-states-with-slowest-price-hikes-in-september/", "final_url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/food-inflation-three-nigerian-states-with-slowest-price-hikes-in-september/", "text": "[Business](https://dailypost.ng/business/)Food Inflation: Three Nigerian states with slowest price hikes in SeptemberPublished on October 16, 2026By [Ogaga Ariemu](https://dailypost.ng/author/ogaga-ariemu/)[Comment](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/food-inflation-three-nigerian-states-with-slowest-price-hikes-in-september/comments/) Adamawa, Kano and Bauchi recorded the slowest month-on-month increases in food inflation among Nigerian states in September 2026, amid rising food price pressures across the country. This is according to the National Bureau of Statistics, NBS, September 2026 Consumer Price Index and Inflation Report. The data showed that food inflation rose at the slowest pace in Adamawa(-13.84 percent), Kano(-11.01 per cent) and Bauchi(-10.21) on a month-on-month basis, indicating relatively slower increases in food prices in the three states during the period under review. Meanwhile, Imo, Ondo and Oyo recorded the highest month-on-month increases in food inflation in September.Recommended[UBA wins N156bn debt recovery suit against Stallion Group, Vaswani Brothers](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/uba-wins-n156bn-debt-recovery-suit-against-stallion-group-vaswani-brothers/)[FG commissions 1MW Solar Mini-Grid, begins construction of 16MW projects in Gombe](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/fg-commissions-1mw-solar-mini-grid-begins-construction-of-16mw-projects-in-gombe/)[Dollar-to-Naira exchange rate Today, October 16, 2026: Naira depreciates against USD to end week on negative note](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/dollar-to-naira-exchange-rate-today-october-16-2026-naira-depreciates-against-usd-to-end-week-on-negative-note/) On a year-on-year basis, Taraba, Yobe and Borno recorded the slowest food inflation rates among states in the country. In contrast, Lagos, Imo and Ondo recorded the highest year-on-year food inflation rates at 33.40 per cent, 33.79 per cent and 31.49 per cent, respectively. The figures highlight differences in food price movements across states, with some locations experiencing slower increases while others continued to face significant food inflation. DAILY POST reports that Nigeria\u2019s headline inflation rate eased to 14.64 per cent in September 2026 from 15.39 per cent in August. However, [food inflation increased slightly](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/15/nigerias-inflation-rate-drops-to-14-64-in-september) to 19.59 per cent in September from 19.57 per cent recorded in the preceding month, indicating that food price pressures persisted despite the decline in the overall inflation rate.Share this story[WhatsApp](https://wa.me/?text=Food%20Inflation%3A%20Three%20Nigerian%20states%20with%20slowest%20price%20hikes%20in%20September%20https%3A%2F%2Fdailypost.ng%2F2026%2F10%2F16%2Ffood-inflation-three-nigerian-states-with-slowest-price-hikes-in-september%2F) Facebook You may like[Inflation: Three Nigerian states with highest food price hikes in September 2026](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/inflation-three-nigerian-states-with-highest-food-price-hikes-in-september-2026/)[IMF chief urges countries to develop policies embedded in AI](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/imf-chief-urges-countries-to-develop-policies-embedded-in-ai/)[Taraba farmers may stop irrigation farming over fuel price surge](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/taraba-farmers-may-stop-irrigation-farming-over-fuel-price-surge/)[Join the conversation](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/food-inflation-three-nigerian-states-with-slowest-price-hikes-in-september/comments/)", "content_hash": "71f2173d79edfe76d38a4fa4b2912621e44d2d2c8316553091c4bf20fd43877a", "domain": "dailypost", "fetched_at": "2026-10-18T04:30:05Z", "language": "en"}, {"id": "1011", "title": "Tinubu explains FG\u2019s removal of universities from IPPIS", "url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/why-we-freed-varsities-from-ippis-recruitment-waivers/", "final_url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/why-we-freed-varsities-from-ippis-recruitment-waivers/", "text": "[News](https://dailypost.ng/hot-news/)Tinubu explains FG\u2019s removal of universities from IPPISPublished on October 17, 2026By [Timi Owolabi](https://dailypost.ng/author/timi-owolabi/)[Comment](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/why-we-freed-varsities-from-ippis-recruitment-waivers/comments/)President Bola Tinubu has explained that the Federal Government removed universities from the Integrated Personnel and Payroll Information System (IPPIS) and the requirement to obtain recruitment waivers to strengthen institutional autonomy and improve efficiency in the university system.Tinubu spoke on Saturday at the maiden convocation ceremony of the Federal University of Health Sciences, Azare (FUHSA), in Bauchi State, where 50 pioneer students graduated from the Department of Human Nutrition and Dietetics.The President, who is the university\u2019s Visitor, was represented by the Executive Secretary of the Tertiary Education Trust Fund (TETFund), Sunny Echono.He said the reforms would allow universities to recruit staff based on their manpower needs without seeking approval from the Office of the Head of the Civil Service of the Federation.Recommended[Veteran journalist Dele Cole dies at 86](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/veteran-journalist-dele-cole-dies-at-86/)[Peter Obi questions why Nigeria did not declare World Poverty Day public holiday](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/peter-obi-questions-why-nigeria-did-not-declare-world-poverty-day-public-holiday/)[Economic growth meaningless if citizens are getting poorer \u2013 Peter Obi slams Tinubu](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/economic-growth-meaningless-if-citizens-are-getting-poorer-peter-obi-slams-tinubu/)\u201cAs part of our commitment to greater institutional efficiency and autonomy, the Federal Government has removed universities from the requirement to obtain recruitment waivers,\u201d Tinubu said.He added that the government had also taken steps to remove universities from IPPIS and develop a payroll system that accommodated the peculiarities of the university system.According to him, the changes were aimed at helping universities attract and retain qualified personnel to improve teaching, research, innovation and national development.Tinubu also disclosed that 1,798 FUHSA students had benefited from the Nigerian Education Loan Fund (NELFUND) for the 2025/2026 academic session, representing 43 per cent of the institution\u2019s student population.He said the initiative was part of the government\u2019s efforts to ensure that financial difficulties did not prevent qualified Nigerians from accessing higher education.The President further disclosed that the Federal Government, through TETFund, had provided N10bn for the National Research Fund in 2026, urging universities, particularly health-related institutions, to use the opportunity to conduct research addressing the country\u2019s health challenges.He said the government was also committed to improving the welfare and professional development of staff in tertiary institutions, while strengthening security through the Safe School Initiative and other measures.Tinubu commended FUHSA for establishing partnerships with international institutions, including the University of Miami, Boston University and Universiti Sains Malaysia.He urged the university to translate the collaborations into practical outcomes that would improve teaching, research, innovation and healthcare delivery.The President congratulated the 50 pioneer graduates, describing their achievement as a significant milestone in the development of the institution, which was established to address gaps in Nigeria\u2019s health sector exposed by the COVID-19 pandemic.In his address, the FUHSA Vice-Chancellor, Prof. Bala Mohammed Audu, said the university had established 22 academic programmes in less than five years.He disclosed that 11 of the 13 programmes that had reached the accreditation stage had received full accreditation, while two had received interim accreditation.Audu said the university had graduated 50 students from its Department of Human Nutrition and Dietetics, including three who obtained first-class degrees.He added that the graduates had developed more than 34 value-added nutritional products during their training, some of which could be commercialised.The vice-chancellor also called for a review of the extension of the nutrition programme from four to five years under the Core Curriculum Minimum Academic Standards, arguing that the four-year programme had adequately equipped students with the required skills.He thanked Bauchi State Governor Bala Mohammed for providing the university\u2019s campus and 600 hectares of land at Dugunde for future expansion.Audu also acknowledged the support of several universities, teaching hospitals and other institutions that provided personnel, classrooms and facilities during FUHSA\u2019s take-off.Share this story[WhatsApp](https://wa.me/?text=Tinubu%20explains%20FG%E2%80%99s%20removal%20of%20universities%20from%20IPPIS%20https%3A%2F%2Fdailypost.ng%2F2026%2F10%2F17%2Fwhy-we-freed-varsities-from-ippis-recruitment-waivers%2F) FacebookYou may like[2027: G-100 coalition reveals when opposition will pick single candidate to face Tinubu](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/2027-g-100-coalition-reveals-when-opposition-will-pick-single-candidate-to-face-tinubu/)[Wrong choices of politicians kept Nigeria like this - Ex-NCDC boss, Ihekweazu charges students not to lose hope](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/wrong-choices-of-politicians-kept-nigeria-like-this-ex-ncdc-boss-ihekweazu-charges-students-not-lose-hope/)['Give us pension increase before you leave office' - Ogun retired principals beg Gov Abiodun](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/give-us-pension-increase-before-you-leave-office-ogun-retired-principals-beg-abiodun/)[Join the conversation](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/why-we-freed-varsities-from-ippis-recruitment-waivers/comments/)", "content_hash": "fccb67ffd3e7d4d3d48756ff77a71ffbc2c0bf8e11a56f12e9ee28299efa341c", "domain": "dailypost", "fetched_at": "2026-10-18T04:30:06Z", "language": "en"}, {"id": "1012", "title": "'Give us pension increase before you leave office' - Ogun retired principals beg Gov Abiodun", "url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/give-us-pension-increase-before-you-leave-office-ogun-retired-principals-beg-abiodun/", "final_url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/give-us-pension-increase-before-you-leave-office-ogun-retired-principals-beg-abiodun/", "text": "[News](https://dailypost.ng/hot-news/)'Give us pension increase before you leave office' - Ogun retired principals beg Gov AbiodunPublished on October 17, 2026By [Gift Oba](https://dailypost.ng/author/gift-oba/)[Comment](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/give-us-pension-increase-before-you-leave-office-ogun-retired-principals-beg-abiodun/comments/)The Association of Retired Principals of Secondary Schools of Nigeria, ARPSSON, Ogun State chapter, has appealed to Governor Dapo Abiodun to implement a consequential increase in pensions before leaving office in 2027.The president of the association, Comrade Segun Obadimu, made the appeal on Friday during its 2026 Annual State Congress held at Graceland Event Centre, Ayepe Road, Sagamu.Obadimu said current pension payments could no longer meet retirees' needs in view of prevailing economic realities.He also urged the governor to clear the backlog of gratuities owed to retirees from 2020 to 2025.Recommended[Veteran journalist Dele Cole dies at 86](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/veteran-journalist-dele-cole-dies-at-86/)[Peter Obi questions why Nigeria did not declare World Poverty Day public holiday](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/peter-obi-questions-why-nigeria-did-not-declare-world-poverty-day-public-holiday/)[Economic growth meaningless if citizens are getting poorer \u2013 Peter Obi slams Tinubu](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/economic-growth-meaningless-if-citizens-are-getting-poorer-peter-obi-slams-tinubu/)\"Our message to Governor Dapo Abiodun, who has been doing well for pensioners, is to actualise the consequential increase in our pensions. What is being paid currently cannot take us anywhere,\" he said.\"We are also requesting that the backlog of gratuities between 2020 and 2025 be cleared. We believe this is doable before 2027,\" Obadimu added.The congress, themed \"Healthy Life in Retirement,\" featured a health talk titled \"Ageing Realities with Special Emphasis on Hypertension and Diabetes.\"Obadimu said the theme was chosen to draw attention to the health and well-being of retired educators. He urged members to undergo regular medical check-ups and adhere to medical advice to reduce the risks associated with hypertension and diabetes.On the 2027 general elections, the ARPSSON president urged members to participate actively and shun violence.\"We have informed our members to go and cast their votes. Our members should participate actively and stay clear of violence,\" he said.Also speaking, the association's Public Relations Officer, Dayo Onabowale, urged members to vote for candidates of their choice.\"As we approach the 2027 elections, I want our members to come out en masse to vote for your trusted candidate so that we can choose a government of our choice,\" he said.The Commissioner for Education, Science and Technology, Abayomi Arigbabu, represented by the Zonal Education Officer, Mr Kola Abolaji, commended the association for organising the congress.Dignitaries at the event included the President of Lagos State ARPSSON, Adegunle Abayomi; the Chairman of the Academic Staff Union of Secondary Schools, ASUSS, Comrade Agbesanwa Seun; and the Deputy Chairman of the Nigeria Union of Teachers (NUT), Ogun State, Comrade Okulalu Olufemi.They urged retired principals to continue playing advisory roles in the education sector.Share this story[WhatsApp](https://wa.me/?text='Give%20us%20pension%20increase%20before%20you%20leave%20office'%20-%20Ogun%20retired%20principals%20beg%20Gov%20Abiodun%20https%3A%2F%2Fdailypost.ng%2F2026%2F10%2F17%2Fgive-us-pension-increase-before-you-leave-office-ogun-retired-principals-beg-abiodun%2F) FacebookYou may like[Wrong choices of politicians kept Nigeria like this - Ex-NCDC boss, Ihekweazu charges students not to lose hope](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/wrong-choices-of-politicians-kept-nigeria-like-this-ex-ncdc-boss-ihekweazu-charges-students-not-lose-hope/)[Tinubu explains FG\u2019s removal of universities from IPPIS](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/why-we-freed-varsities-from-ippis-recruitment-waivers/)['We will protect valid votes in Kogi LG election\u2019 \u2013 KOSIEC Chairman](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/kogi-lg-poll-kosiec-vows-ro-protect-valid-votes/)[Join the conversation](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/give-us-pension-increase-before-you-leave-office-ogun-retired-principals-beg-abiodun/comments/)", "content_hash": "c2480dae48ba0523b5b44e68f1d81f79d4b54fbbfa536cf22d9acdb23c62a0bb", "domain": "dailypost", "fetched_at": "2026-10-18T04:30:08Z", "language": "en"}, {"id": "1013", "title": "Nurse dies during asthma attack at Ogun psychiatric hospital as colleague alleges oxygen failure", "url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/nurse-dies-during-asthma-attack-at-ogun-psychiatric-hospital-as-colleague-alleges-oxygen-failure/", "final_url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/nurse-dies-during-asthma-attack-at-ogun-psychiatric-hospital-as-colleague-alleges-oxygen-failure/", "text": "[Metro](https://dailypost.ng/metro/)Nurse dies during asthma attack at Ogun psychiatric hospital as colleague alleges oxygen failurePublished on October 17, 2026By [Gift Oba](https://dailypost.ng/author/gift-oba/)[Comment](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/nurse-dies-during-asthma-attack-at-ogun-psychiatric-hospital-as-colleague-alleges-oxygen-failure/comments/)A nurse identified as Taiwo Godwin Ayodeji has died after suffering an asthma attack at the Federal Neuropsychiatric Hospital, Aro, Abeokuta, Ogun State, sparking outrage over alleged medical negligence.Ayodeji, a post-basic nursing student at the School of Nursing, Aro, was said to be a known asthma patient.According to an eyewitness account, Ayodeji developed breathing difficulties while playing football and was rushed to the hospital's emergency unit.A friend who accompanied him said the deceased was still able to walk into the facility on arrival.Recommended[Troops kill two suspected kidnappers, rescue victim, recover N10m ransom in Kano](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/troops-gun-down-two-kidnappers-rescue-one-recover-n10m-ransom-in-kano/)['Give us pension increase before you leave office' - Ogun retired principals beg Gov Abiodun](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/give-us-pension-increase-before-you-leave-office-ogun-retired-principals-beg-abiodun/)[Police arrest three men over alleged homosexual acts in Oyo](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/oyo-police-arrest-three-men-over-alleged-sodomy/)The eyewitness, however, alleged that although Ayodeji was placed on oxygen equipment, the oxygen supply was not turned on.\u201cI noticed he was on oxygen, but the oxygen was not put on,\u201d the source was quoted as saying.The source further alleged that by the time the medical team attended to him, his condition had deteriorated, with a weak pulse and dilated pupils. Efforts to secure his airway were reportedly unsuccessful before he was pronounced dead.The eyewitness also alleged that Ayodeji's death was the second time a nurse from the same school had died at the facility this year, raising concerns among colleagues and students.Reacting to the incident, the management of the Federal Neuropsychiatric Hospital, Aro, confirmed the death and announced an investigation.In a press statement signed by the Public Relations Officer, Ajibola Joseph Oluwatoyin Abiola, on behalf of the Acting Provost and Medical Director on Saturday, the hospital said it was deeply saddened by the untimely death of Mr Taiwo Godwin while receiving care at its General Medical Practice Unit, GMPU.\u201cThe management extends its heartfelt condolences to the bereaved family, friends, colleagues, fellow students, and the entire nursing community over this painful loss,\u201d the statement said.The hospital assured students, staff and the public that an investigation into the circumstances surrounding the incident was ongoing, promising that it would be thorough, impartial and transparent.It urged the public to remain calm and allow the investigation to proceed.\u201cWe remain committed to patient safety, professional accountability and the highest standards of care,\u201d the statement added.Share this story[WhatsApp](https://wa.me/?text=Nurse%20dies%20during%20asthma%20attack%20at%20Ogun%20psychiatric%20hospital%20as%20colleague%20alleges%20oxygen%20failure%20https%3A%2F%2Fdailypost.ng%2F2026%2F10%2F17%2Fnurse-dies-during-asthma-attack-at-ogun-psychiatric-hospital-as-colleague-alleges-oxygen-failure%2F) FacebookYou may like[Gunmen kill three police officers in Zamfara](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/bandits-kill-three-policemen-in-zamfara-night-attack/)[Osun Amotekun arrests five suspects over alleged criminal activities](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/osun-amotekun-arrests-five-suspects-over-alleged-criminal-activities/)[Oyo: Police arrest three men over alleged homosexual acts](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/oyo-police-arrest-three-men-over-alleged-homosexual-acts/)[Join the conversation](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/nurse-dies-during-asthma-attack-at-ogun-psychiatric-hospital-as-colleague-alleges-oxygen-failure/comments/)", "content_hash": "0343bb087110b3b2d4533cc1db501c336508b16061102b841f88f4f76e363a7b", "domain": "dailypost", "fetched_at": "2026-10-18T04:30:09Z", "language": "en"}, {"id": "1014", "title": "Police arrest three men over alleged homosexual acts in Oyo", "url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/oyo-police-arrest-three-men-over-alleged-sodomy/", "final_url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/oyo-police-arrest-three-men-over-alleged-sodomy/", "text": "[Metro](https://dailypost.ng/metro/)Police arrest three men over alleged homosexual acts in OyoPublished on October 17, 2026By [Kabeer Bello](https://dailypost.ng/author/kabeer-bello/)[Comment](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/oyo-police-arrest-three-men-over-alleged-sodomy/comments/)The Oyo State Police Command has arrested three men in Saki over alleged homosexual acts following an intelligence report received by the authorities.The suspects were identified as Ayomide Lukeman, 22; Shuaib Aremu, 22; and Abdul-Rasheed Mufeed, 23.The command\u2019s spokesperson, Ayanlade Olayinka, announced the arrests in a statement issued on Friday, October 16, 2026.According to the police, the command received intelligence on September 29 alleging that a group of individuals was involved in what it described as \"unnatural sexual conduct.\"Recommended[Troops kill two suspected kidnappers, rescue victim, recover N10m ransom in Kano](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/troops-gun-down-two-kidnappers-rescue-one-recover-n10m-ransom-in-kano/)[Nurse dies during asthma attack at Ogun psychiatric hospital as colleague alleges oxygen failure](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/nurse-dies-during-asthma-attack-at-ogun-psychiatric-hospital-as-colleague-alleges-oxygen-failure/)[2027 elections: Kano police warn against fake news, boast of robust security](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/2027-elections-kano-police-warn-against-fake-news-assure-robust-security/)The Commissioner of Police subsequently directed the Monitoring Unit to investigate the report and take the necessary action, leading to the arrest of the three men by operatives attached to the unit\u2019s Saki operational base.The police said preliminary investigations suggested that the suspects had engaged in homosexual acts.\"Specifically, two of the suspects reportedly confessed to having had carnal knowledge of the third suspect on multiple occasions, with the latter allegedly regarded by them as their 'wife',\" the statement said.The command said investigations were continuing to establish the circumstances surrounding the allegations and determine whether other individuals were involved.\"The Command assures the public that all necessary investigative procedures will be followed to establish the facts and ensure that appropriate action is taken based on the outcome of the investigation,\" the statement added.The police urged members of the public to provide timely and credible information to support efforts to prevent, detect and investigate crime.Share this story[WhatsApp](https://wa.me/?text=Police%20arrest%20three%20men%20over%20alleged%20homosexual%20acts%20in%20Oyo%20https%3A%2F%2Fdailypost.ng%2F2026%2F10%2F17%2Foyo-police-arrest-three-men-over-alleged-sodomy%2F) FacebookYou may like[Gunmen kill three police officers in Zamfara](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/bandits-kill-three-policemen-in-zamfara-night-attack/)[Osun Amotekun arrests five suspects over alleged criminal activities](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/osun-amotekun-arrests-five-suspects-over-alleged-criminal-activities/)[Oyo: Police arrest three men over alleged homosexual acts](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/oyo-police-arrest-three-men-over-alleged-homosexual-acts/)[Join the conversation](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/oyo-police-arrest-three-men-over-alleged-sodomy/comments/)", "content_hash": "5fee88d997490d1acc29d6246021decfcceafb7696187c618dba11650f0d71e0", "domain": "dailypost", "fetched_at": "2026-10-18T04:30:11Z", "language": "en"}, {"id": "1015", "title": "Gunmen kill three police officers in Zamfara", "url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/bandits-kill-three-policemen-in-zamfara-night-attack/", "final_url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/bandits-kill-three-policemen-in-zamfara-night-attack/", "text": "[Metro](https://dailypost.ng/metro/)Gunmen kill three police officers in ZamfaraPublished on October 17, 2026By [Hafsat Bello](https://dailypost.ng/author/hafsat-bello/)[Comment](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/bandits-kill-three-policemen-in-zamfara-night-attack/comments/)At least three police officers have reportedly lost their lives after gunmen attacked a patrol team in Gusau, the Zamfara State capital.The incident reportedly took place at about 2 am on Saturday in the Damba Division, while the officers were carrying out night patrol duties, according to SaharaReporters.A source familiar with the incident told the publication, that the officers were caught off guard by the attackers.The source said the assailants opened fire on the patrol team, leaving the police vehicle riddled with bullets.Recommended[Troops kill two suspected kidnappers, rescue victim, recover N10m ransom in Kano](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/troops-gun-down-two-kidnappers-rescue-one-recover-n10m-ransom-in-kano/)[Nurse dies during asthma attack at Ogun psychiatric hospital as colleague alleges oxygen failure](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/nurse-dies-during-asthma-attack-at-ogun-psychiatric-hospital-as-colleague-alleges-oxygen-failure/)[Police arrest three men over alleged homosexual acts in Oyo](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/oyo-police-arrest-three-men-over-alleged-sodomy/)The circumstances surrounding the attack remain unclear.The Zamfara State Police Command had not issued an official statement on the incident as of the time of filing this report.Share this story[WhatsApp](https://wa.me/?text=Gunmen%20kill%20three%20police%20officers%20in%20Zamfara%20https%3A%2F%2Fdailypost.ng%2F2026%2F10%2F17%2Fbandits-kill-three-policemen-in-zamfara-night-attack%2F) FacebookYou may like[Osun Amotekun arrests five suspects over alleged criminal activities](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/osun-amotekun-arrests-five-suspects-over-alleged-criminal-activities/)[Oyo: Police arrest three men over alleged homosexual acts](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/oyo-police-arrest-three-men-over-alleged-homosexual-acts/)[Bauchi court jails eight over thuggery in Unguwar Dim](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/bauchi-court-jails-eight-over-thuggery-in-unguwar-dim/)[Join the conversation](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/bandits-kill-three-policemen-in-zamfara-night-attack/comments/)", "content_hash": "cec6a4f599f72b54c1c9fcb1e126a9bcb77779d262d757d56e08ee20eb524cf7", "domain": "dailypost", "fetched_at": "2026-10-18T04:30:12Z", "language": "en"}, {"id": "1016", "title": "Osun Amotekun arrests five suspects over alleged criminal activities", "url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/osun-amotekun-arrests-five-suspects-over-alleged-criminal-activities/", "final_url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/osun-amotekun-arrests-five-suspects-over-alleged-criminal-activities/", "text": "[Metro](https://dailypost.ng/metro/)Osun Amotekun arrests five suspects over alleged criminal activitiesPublished on October 17, 2026By [Francis Ezediuno](https://dailypost.ng/author/francis-ezediuno/)[Comment](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/osun-amotekun-arrests-five-suspects-over-alleged-criminal-activities/comments/) The Osun Amotekun Corps has arrested five suspects over alleged theft, conspiracy, shop burglary and fraud in different locations across the state. The suspects were identified as 30-year-old Adebisi Olalere; 33-year-old Isiaka Yinusa; 30-year-old Farika Azeez; 30-year-old Daniel Moses and 30-year-old Monday Lawrence. According to a statement issued on Saturday by the Corps\u2019 Public Relations Officer, CSA Yusuf Idowu Abass, the suspects were arrested on Wednesday, October 14, 2026, following complaints about their alleged activities. The statement said Corps Commander, Adekunle Isaac Omoyele, said operatives acted on the complaints and apprehended the suspects at different locations, including their alleged hideouts and scenes of reported offences.Recommended[Troops kill two suspected kidnappers, rescue victim, recover N10m ransom in Kano](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/troops-gun-down-two-kidnappers-rescue-one-recover-n10m-ransom-in-kano/)[Nurse dies during asthma attack at Ogun psychiatric hospital as colleague alleges oxygen failure](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/nurse-dies-during-asthma-attack-at-ogun-psychiatric-hospital-as-colleague-alleges-oxygen-failure/)[Police arrest three men over alleged homosexual acts in Oyo](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/oyo-police-arrest-three-men-over-alleged-sodomy/) \u201cOlalere, a herbalist from Gbongan, was arrested over allegations that he conspired with armed robbers and supplied them with traditional charms intended to assist their criminal activities. \u201cHe was reportedly arrested alongside Yinusa, also from Gbongan, who was apprehended in connection with an alleged shop burglary in the town. \u201cYinusa is a former convict who had previously served a prison sentence for motorcycle theft. Both men allegedly admitted involvement in the offences during preliminary investigations,\u201d the statement disclosed. In a separate incident, Azeez, from Modakeke, was arrested over the alleged theft of a gas cylinder and other items in the community. The Corps said Azeez had previously been convicted of a similar offence and had served a jail term. He allegedly admitted to the latest incident during interrogation. \u201cMoses and Lawrence, both 30-year-old men from Benue State residing in Ipinrindo, Atakumosa East Local Government Area, were arrested over the alleged theft of iron rods from the local government secretariat. \u201cMoses allegedly admitted participating in the theft and said the stolen iron rods, estimated to be worth between N50,000 and N100,000, were sold to scrap dealers for between N4,000 and N5,000,\u201d the statement added. Omoyele said preliminary investigations had produced admissions from some of the suspects, while some had reportedly identified other individuals allegedly connected with the incidents. The Corps commander urged residents to provide credible and timely information to security agencies to help prevent crime and address potential security threats across Osun State. \u201cThe five suspects have been handed over to the appropriate authorities for further investigation and possible prosecution,\u201d the statement added..Share this story[WhatsApp](https://wa.me/?text=Osun%20Amotekun%20arrests%20five%20suspects%20over%20alleged%20criminal%20activities%20https%3A%2F%2Fdailypost.ng%2F2026%2F10%2F17%2Fosun-amotekun-arrests-five-suspects-over-alleged-criminal-activities%2F) Facebook You may like[Gunmen kill three police officers in Zamfara](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/bandits-kill-three-policemen-in-zamfara-night-attack/)[Oyo: Police arrest three men over alleged homosexual acts](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/oyo-police-arrest-three-men-over-alleged-homosexual-acts/)[Bauchi court jails eight over thuggery in Unguwar Dim](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/bauchi-court-jails-eight-over-thuggery-in-unguwar-dim/)[Join the conversation](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/osun-amotekun-arrests-five-suspects-over-alleged-criminal-activities/comments/)", "content_hash": "c978f4ebb01ae606c1d2200cf062ec47b3433f787356c27e0435db8aa2929100", "domain": "dailypost", "fetched_at": "2026-10-18T04:30:13Z", "language": "en"}, {"id": "1017", "title": "Oyo: Police arrest three men over alleged homosexual acts", "url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/oyo-police-arrest-three-men-over-alleged-homosexual-acts/", "final_url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/oyo-police-arrest-three-men-over-alleged-homosexual-acts/", "text": "[Metro](https://dailypost.ng/metro/)Oyo: Police arrest three men over alleged homosexual actsPublished on October 17, 2026By [Sunday Dennis](https://dailypost.ng/author/sunday-dennis/)[Comment](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/oyo-police-arrest-three-men-over-alleged-homosexual-acts/comments/) Police operatives in Oyo State have arrested three men in Saki over allegations of engaging in same-sex acts. The suspects were identified as Ayomide Lukeman, 22, Shuaib Aremu, 22, and Abdul-Rasheed Mufeed, 23. They were apprehended by operatives of the Oyo State Police Command Monitoring Unit, Saki Operational Base. The command\u2019s spokesperson, DSP Olayinka Ayanlade, said the arrests followed intelligence received on September 29, 2026, regarding the alleged involvement of some individuals in what the police described as unnatural sexual conduct. According to Ayanlade, the Commissioner of Police directed the Monitoring Unit to investigate the information and take appropriate action, leading to the arrest of the three suspects.Recommended[Troops kill two suspected kidnappers, rescue victim, recover N10m ransom in Kano](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/troops-gun-down-two-kidnappers-rescue-one-recover-n10m-ransom-in-kano/)[Nurse dies during asthma attack at Ogun psychiatric hospital as colleague alleges oxygen failure](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/nurse-dies-during-asthma-attack-at-ogun-psychiatric-hospital-as-colleague-alleges-oxygen-failure/)[Police arrest three men over alleged homosexual acts in Oyo](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/oyo-police-arrest-three-men-over-alleged-sodomy/) \u201cUpon receipt of the information, the Commissioner of Police, Oyo State Command, directed the Command Monitoring Unit to verify the intelligence and take appropriate action, culminating in the arrest of three suspects,\u201d he said. The police spokesperson added that preliminary investigations indicated that the suspects had allegedly admitted to engaging in homosexual acts. He said two of the men allegedly confessed to having had sexual relations with the third suspect on several occasions, adding that they reportedly referred to the latter as their \u201cwife\u201d. Ayanlade stated that investigations were continuing to establish the circumstances surrounding the allegations and determine whether other individuals were involved. He reiterated the command\u2019s commitment to conducting the investigation professionally, impartially and in accordance with the law, assuring the public that appropriate action would be taken based on the findings. Nigeria\u2019s Same-Sex Marriage (Prohibition) Act, 2013, criminalises same-sex marriages and civil unions, while other provisions of the law prohibit certain same-sex relationships and activities. The law prescribes penalties of up to 14 years\u2019 imprisonment for individuals convicted of entering into a same-sex marriage or civil union.Share this story[WhatsApp](https://wa.me/?text=Oyo%3A%20Police%20arrest%20three%20men%20over%20alleged%20homosexual%20acts%20https%3A%2F%2Fdailypost.ng%2F2026%2F10%2F17%2Foyo-police-arrest-three-men-over-alleged-homosexual-acts%2F) Facebook You may like[2027 elections: Kano police warn against fake news, boast of robust security](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/2027-elections-kano-police-warn-against-fake-news-assure-robust-security/)[Gunmen kill three police officers in Zamfara](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/bandits-kill-three-policemen-in-zamfara-night-attack/)[Osun Amotekun arrests five suspects over alleged criminal activities](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/osun-amotekun-arrests-five-suspects-over-alleged-criminal-activities/)[Join the conversation](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/oyo-police-arrest-three-men-over-alleged-homosexual-acts/comments/)", "content_hash": "00451f4e64308d24e53e95b4358816740d146042f5c0da56a37c8ce22705b4db", "domain": "dailypost", "fetched_at": "2026-10-18T04:30:15Z", "language": "en"}, {"id": "1018", "title": "\u2018Nigerians now have culture of begging\u2019 \u2013 Omotola Jalade", "url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/nigerians-now-have-culture-of-begging-omotola-jalade/", "final_url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/nigerians-now-have-culture-of-begging-omotola-jalade/", "text": "[Entertainment](https://dailypost.ng/entertainment/)\u2018Nigerians now have culture of begging\u2019 \u2013 Omotola JaladePublished on October 17, 2026By [Sunny Green Itodo](https://dailypost.ng/author/sunny-green-itodo/)[Comment](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/nigerians-now-have-culture-of-begging-omotola-jalade/comments/)Veteran Nigerian actress, Omotola Jalade Ekeinde has criticised the entitlement mentality of the Nigerian society, lamenting that the country now has a culture of begging. Speaking in a recent episode of Activating Success With Love Idoko, the movie icon said she doesn\u2019t support or encourage begging in any form except if it is a life-and-death situation. According to her, there is no reason anyone can\u2019t work. She said, \u201cA lot of Nigerians take opportunities for granted. And one thing we have to understand is that nobody owes you anything. Nigerians now have a culture of begging.Recommended[I panicked after Davido stopped talking to me \u2013 Mayorkun](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/i-panicked-after-davido-stopped-talking-to-me-mayorkun/)[\u2018I defeated 17 Governors, won\u2019t support APC\u2019 \u2013 Davido](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/i-defeated-17-governors-wont-support-apc-davido/)[I\u2019ve never been an advocate for marriage \u2013 Uzor Arukwe](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/ive-never-been-an-advocate-for-marriage-uzor-arukwe/) \u201cI don\u2019t support or encourage begging. I believe that there is no reason why anybody can\u2019t work. There is something you can do. There is a kind of value you can bring to humanity. \u201cEverybody has needs, including me. There are some needs I have that if I was entitled I would go and beg certain people. \u201cSo, don\u2019t feel like because you don\u2019t have money like me, you are the only one who has a reason to beg. At every level, we all have needs. But we are all struggling through it. Even if you have to beg, it should be a life-and-death situation.\u201d Omotola added, \u201cTry as much as you can not to beg and be a nuisance. Begging reduces your own self-worth. If you must beg, let it be in a desperate situation. And don\u2019t do it with entitlement.\u201dShare this story[WhatsApp](https://wa.me/?text=%E2%80%98Nigerians%20now%20have%20culture%20of%20begging%E2%80%99%20%E2%80%93%20Omotola%20Jalade%20https%3A%2F%2Fdailypost.ng%2F2026%2F10%2F17%2Fnigerians-now-have-culture-of-begging-omotola-jalade%2F) Facebook You may like[Nathaniel Bassey reacts to death of gospel singer, Toluwanisings](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/nathaniel-bassey-reacts-to-death-of-gospel-singer-toluwanisings/)[Tope Alabi, Yinka Alaseyori, Bidemi Olaoba, Ebuka Songs mourn gospel singer, Toluwanisings](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/tope-alabi-yinka-alaseyori-bidemi-olaoba-ebuka-songs-mourn-gospel-singer-toluwanisings/)[Gehgeh accuses VDM of threatening Davido over Burna Boy feud](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/gehgeh-accuses-vdm-of-threatening-davido-over-burna-boy-feud/)[Join the conversation](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/nigerians-now-have-culture-of-begging-omotola-jalade/comments/)", "content_hash": "942d311d44bd5796fe74b91a4a0fc934371e27adea0971a7fd35e80fd7c68e39", "domain": "dailypost", "fetched_at": "2026-10-18T04:30:16Z", "language": "en"}, {"id": "1019", "title": "I panicked after Davido stopped talking to me \u2013 Mayorkun", "url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/i-panicked-after-davido-stopped-talking-to-me-mayorkun/", "final_url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/i-panicked-after-davido-stopped-talking-to-me-mayorkun/", "text": "[Entertainment](https://dailypost.ng/entertainment/)I panicked after Davido stopped talking to me \u2013 MayorkunPublished on October 17, 2026By [Sunny Green Itodo](https://dailypost.ng/author/sunny-green-itodo/)[Comment](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/i-panicked-after-davido-stopped-talking-to-me-mayorkun/comments/) Nigerian singer, Adewale Mayowa Emmanuel, popularly known as Mayorkun, has shared how Davido \u201cmiraculously\u201d messaged and signed him after snubbing him for two weeks. Speaking in a recent episode of the Afropolitan podcast, Mayorkun explained that he had quit his banking job after Davido promised to sign him after seeing a clip of him singing online, but the DMW ghosted him for two weeks, which left him in panic. Mayorkun said he resorted to seeking spiritual assistance and started going to church, trusting God to intervene. He recalled that after leading a praise and worship session in the church one day, Davido texted him immediately and asked him to move into his house. Recommended[\u2018Nigerians now have culture of begging\u2019 \u2013 Omotola Jalade](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/nigerians-now-have-culture-of-begging-omotola-jalade/)[\u2018I defeated 17 Governors, won\u2019t support APC\u2019 \u2013 Davido](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/i-defeated-17-governors-wont-support-apc-davido/)[I\u2019ve never been an advocate for marriage \u2013 Uzor Arukwe](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/ive-never-been-an-advocate-for-marriage-uzor-arukwe/) \u201cDavido stopped replying to me for two weeks after I quit my banking job. I started going to church, and one day, immediately after singing praise and worship, he texted me on WhatsApp to pack my luggage and come to his house. It was more than a testimony. \u201cYou may not believe me but I haven\u2019t even returned to my seat after leading the praise and worship before he messaged. I was on my way to my seat. Before then, I was in panic because I wasn\u2019t sure whether Davido would talk to me again,\u201d he stated.Share this story[WhatsApp](https://wa.me/?text=I%20panicked%20after%20Davido%20stopped%20talking%20to%20me%20%E2%80%93%20Mayorkun%20https%3A%2F%2Fdailypost.ng%2F2026%2F10%2F17%2Fi-panicked-after-davido-stopped-talking-to-me-mayorkun%2F) Facebook You may like[Nathaniel Bassey reacts to death of gospel singer, Toluwanisings](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/nathaniel-bassey-reacts-to-death-of-gospel-singer-toluwanisings/)[Tope Alabi, Yinka Alaseyori, Bidemi Olaoba, Ebuka Songs mourn gospel singer, Toluwanisings](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/tope-alabi-yinka-alaseyori-bidemi-olaoba-ebuka-songs-mourn-gospel-singer-toluwanisings/)[Gehgeh accuses VDM of threatening Davido over Burna Boy feud](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/gehgeh-accuses-vdm-of-threatening-davido-over-burna-boy-feud/)[Join the conversation](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/i-panicked-after-davido-stopped-talking-to-me-mayorkun/comments/)", "content_hash": "b09e87de8b63bdbbb762c18195d7dddaf1f5629ca763078749b810023d3fba1c", "domain": "dailypost", "fetched_at": "2026-10-18T04:30:17Z", "language": "en"}, {"id": "1020", "title": "\u2018I defeated 17 Governors, won\u2019t support APC\u2019 \u2013 Davido", "url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/i-defeated-17-governors-wont-support-apc-davido/", "final_url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/i-defeated-17-governors-wont-support-apc-davido/", "text": "[Entertainment](https://dailypost.ng/entertainment/)\u2018I defeated 17 Governors, won\u2019t support APC\u2019 \u2013 DavidoPublished on October 16, 2026By [Vanessa Onah](https://dailypost.ng/author/vanessa-onah/)[Comment](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/i-defeated-17-governors-wont-support-apc-davido/comments/) Popular Nigerian singer David Adeleke, popularly known as Davido, has ruled out supporting the All Progressives Congress, APC, ahead of the 2027 presidential election, despite his uncle, Osun State Governor Ademola Adeleke, endorsing President Bola Tinubu. In a recent video making the rounds online, the Grammy-nominated artist made his position known during an interview with News Central TV, just days after the Osun State governorship election and the announcement of the results. The singer explained that although his uncle, Governor Ademola Adeleke, declared support for President Bola Tinubu after winning the election, he was not obligated to follow his uncle\u2019s political choice. He also recalled his involvement in previous political campaigns, including his support for former Vice-President Atiku Abubakar when they were in the Peoples Democratic Party (PDP).Recommended[2027: No vacancy in Aso Rock, North will vote 100 per cent for Tinubu - Kano Gov, Yusuf](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/2027-no-vacancy-in-aso-rock-north-will-vote-100-for-tinubu-kano-gov-yusuf-2/)[2027: G-100 coalition reveals when opposition will pick single candidate to face Tinubu](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/2027-g-100-coalition-reveals-when-opposition-will-pick-single-candidate-to-face-tinubu/)[2027: NDC candidate raises alarm over alleged plot to remove party from ballot in Lagos](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/2027-ndc-candidate-raises-alarm-over-alleged-plot-to-remove-party-from-ballot-in-lagos-2/) Davido said, \u201cI defeated 17 governors with all their power, with all their immunity, escort commanders, DSS, with all their billions. I defeated them with just a phone. \u201cFor now, I feel like I did what I had to do for the Osun people and my family. \u201cYou can\u2019t force me to have a presidential candidate. My uncle might have his personal reasons for the gain of the state.\u201d Speaking about his uncle\u2019s decision to support Tinubu, the singer said, \u201cMy uncle, immediately he won, came out to declare his support for President Tinubu. But as for me, I am not prepared to support anybody. \u201cI personally haven\u2019t seen anybody in the past. Yes, I have supported Atiku before when we were in PDP, and I even supported in 2015 when APC first did the merger. My late uncle was part of the APC, so I campaigned then. \u201cBut right now, I don\u2019t have a presidential candidate. It might change, sha. It\u2019s not going to be APC, but everybody should have their own,\u201d he said.Share this story[WhatsApp](https://wa.me/?text=%E2%80%98I%20defeated%2017%20Governors%2C%20won%E2%80%99t%20support%20APC%E2%80%99%20%E2%80%93%20Davido%20https%3A%2F%2Fdailypost.ng%2F2026%2F10%2F16%2Fi-defeated-17-governors-wont-support-apc-davido%2F) Facebook You may like[Yobe APC unveils 27-member campaign council for 2027 elections [See List]](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/yobe-apc-unveils-27-member-campaign-council-for-2027-names-kaigama-umar-dg-see-list-2/)[APC reinstates suspended Jigawa federal lawmaker](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/jigawa-apc-lifts-suspension-of-federal-lawmaker/)[2027: Tinubu an absentee President not fit for re-election - Kenneth Okonkwo](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/tinubu-cannot-meet-nigerians-directly-kenneth-okonkwo/)[Join the conversation](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/i-defeated-17-governors-wont-support-apc-davido/comments/)", "content_hash": "57d1a70a191de27624bb90c2837a213ce21e7d1af6d343e1a80e2c20ca2b1c2d", "domain": "dailypost", "fetched_at": "2026-10-18T04:30:19Z", "language": "en"}, {"id": "1021", "title": "I\u2019ve never been an advocate for marriage \u2013 Uzor Arukwe", "url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/ive-never-been-an-advocate-for-marriage-uzor-arukwe/", "final_url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/ive-never-been-an-advocate-for-marriage-uzor-arukwe/", "text": "[Entertainment](https://dailypost.ng/entertainment/)I\u2019ve never been an advocate for marriage \u2013 Uzor ArukwePublished on October 16, 2026By [Roseline Nwosu](https://dailypost.ng/author/roseline-nwosu/)[Comment](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/ive-never-been-an-advocate-for-marriage-uzor-arukwe/comments/) Nollywood actor, Uzor Arukwe, has shared his views on marriage, stating that he has never been a strong advocate for the institution because he believes women bear more responsibilities and challenges in the union. The actor made this known during an interview on the In My Opinion podcast, where he discussed societal expectations surrounding marriage and the pressure often placed on women. According to Arukwe, women go through pregnancy and childbirth, take their husbands\u2019 surnames and shoulder several other responsibilities associated with building a family. He explained that these demands have influenced his perspective on marriage, adding that society is gradually recognising that a woman\u2019s identity and worth are not defined by her marital status.Recommended[\u2018Nigerians now have culture of begging\u2019 \u2013 Omotola Jalade](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/nigerians-now-have-culture-of-begging-omotola-jalade/)[I panicked after Davido stopped talking to me \u2013 Mayorkun](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/i-panicked-after-davido-stopped-talking-to-me-mayorkun/)[\u2018I defeated 17 Governors, won\u2019t support APC\u2019 \u2013 Davido](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/i-defeated-17-governors-wont-support-apc-davido/) He said: \u201cI\u2019ve never really been an advocate for marriage because I feel like it is more tasking for the woman. She\u2019s the one who bears the children, takes the man\u2019s last name, and has to deal with a lot of things. So, I feel society is now beginning to catch on to the fact that marriage doesn\u2019t define or make a woman. \u201cGrowing up, people would ask you why you weren\u2019t married at 25 or 30 and talk about how they already had five children by that age. Now, there are even women who don\u2019t want to have children. I\u2019ve met at least two or three.\u201dShare this story[WhatsApp](https://wa.me/?text=I%E2%80%99ve%20never%20been%20an%20advocate%20for%20marriage%20%E2%80%93%20Uzor%20Arukwe%20https%3A%2F%2Fdailypost.ng%2F2026%2F10%2F16%2Five-never-been-an-advocate-for-marriage-uzor-arukwe%2F) Facebook You may like[Nathaniel Bassey reacts to death of gospel singer, Toluwanisings](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/nathaniel-bassey-reacts-to-death-of-gospel-singer-toluwanisings/)[Tope Alabi, Yinka Alaseyori, Bidemi Olaoba, Ebuka Songs mourn gospel singer, Toluwanisings](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/tope-alabi-yinka-alaseyori-bidemi-olaoba-ebuka-songs-mourn-gospel-singer-toluwanisings/)[Gehgeh accuses VDM of threatening Davido over Burna Boy feud](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/gehgeh-accuses-vdm-of-threatening-davido-over-burna-boy-feud/)[Join the conversation](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/ive-never-been-an-advocate-for-marriage-uzor-arukwe/comments/)", "content_hash": "39b9fe02f10e721d78c9ea6060d0e9b2e52ecedcd90982fa5196903d14dc7301", "domain": "dailypost", "fetched_at": "2026-10-18T04:30:20Z", "language": "en"}, {"id": "1022", "title": "Nathaniel Bassey reacts to death of gospel singer, Toluwanisings", "url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/nathaniel-bassey-reacts-to-death-of-gospel-singer-toluwanisings/", "final_url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/nathaniel-bassey-reacts-to-death-of-gospel-singer-toluwanisings/", "text": "[Entertainment](https://dailypost.ng/entertainment/)Nathaniel Bassey reacts to death of gospel singer, ToluwanisingsPublished on October 16, 2026By [Racheal Ayodele](https://dailypost.ng/author/racheal-ayodele/)[Comment](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/nathaniel-bassey-reacts-to-death-of-gospel-singer-toluwanisings/comments/) Nigerian gospel singer and pastor, Nathaniel Bassey, has reacted to the death of music minister, Toluwanisings. DAILY POST reports that [Toluwanisings slumped and died](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/14/gospel-singer-toluwanisings-is-dead) on Wednesday after being rejected by eight hospitals. Following reports on the circumstances surrounding his death, netizens have called out government over the country\u2019s poor health system while some attached his death to spiritual attack. Reacting to the development in an Instagram post on Friday, Bassey, who said he never met Toluwanisings, explained that he has heard of his great ministration.Recommended[\u2018Nigerians now have culture of begging\u2019 \u2013 Omotola Jalade](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/nigerians-now-have-culture-of-begging-omotola-jalade/)[I panicked after Davido stopped talking to me \u2013 Mayorkun](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/i-panicked-after-davido-stopped-talking-to-me-mayorkun/)[\u2018I defeated 17 Governors, won\u2019t support APC\u2019 \u2013 Davido](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/i-defeated-17-governors-wont-support-apc-davido/) Expressing sadness, Bassey stated that the deceased is now in a better place with God. \u201cSeen and heard about the passing of this brother, Tolusings. Not someone I\u2019ve met before. But I\u2019ve heard how well and great He was doing in His music ministry. Always painful to hear and see young people pass at their prime. \u201cBut as a child of God we believe He is in a better place. I pray strength and comfort for His immediate family, friends and loved ones. It is well, in Jesus\u2019 name,\u201d Bassey stated.Share this story[WhatsApp](https://wa.me/?text=Nathaniel%20Bassey%20reacts%20to%20death%20of%20gospel%20singer%2C%20Toluwanisings%20https%3A%2F%2Fdailypost.ng%2F2026%2F10%2F16%2Fnathaniel-bassey-reacts-to-death-of-gospel-singer-toluwanisings%2F) Facebook You may like[I\u2019ve never been an advocate for marriage \u2013 Uzor Arukwe](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/ive-never-been-an-advocate-for-marriage-uzor-arukwe/)[Tope Alabi, Yinka Alaseyori, Bidemi Olaoba, Ebuka Songs mourn gospel singer, Toluwanisings](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/tope-alabi-yinka-alaseyori-bidemi-olaoba-ebuka-songs-mourn-gospel-singer-toluwanisings/)[Gehgeh accuses VDM of threatening Davido over Burna Boy feud](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/gehgeh-accuses-vdm-of-threatening-davido-over-burna-boy-feud/)[Join the conversation](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/nathaniel-bassey-reacts-to-death-of-gospel-singer-toluwanisings/comments/)", "content_hash": "0581e26dd9e28c5646d46dc3b866d291459c0414759ce90c9d2296156bcef631", "domain": "dailypost", "fetched_at": "2026-10-18T04:30:21Z", "language": "en"}, {"id": "1023", "title": "Tope Alabi, Yinka Alaseyori, Bidemi Olaoba, Ebuka Songs mourn gospel singer, Toluwanisings", "url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/tope-alabi-yinka-alaseyori-bidemi-olaoba-ebuka-songs-mourn-gospel-singer-toluwanisings/", "final_url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/tope-alabi-yinka-alaseyori-bidemi-olaoba-ebuka-songs-mourn-gospel-singer-toluwanisings/", "text": "[Entertainment](https://dailypost.ng/entertainment/)Tope Alabi, Yinka Alaseyori, Bidemi Olaoba, Ebuka Songs mourn gospel singer, ToluwanisingsPublished on October 16, 2026By [Racheal Ayodele](https://dailypost.ng/author/racheal-ayodele/)[Comment](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/tope-alabi-yinka-alaseyori-bidemi-olaoba-ebuka-songs-mourn-gospel-singer-toluwanisings/comments/) Nigerian gospel singers, Tope Alabi, Yinka Alaseyori, Bidemi Olaoba, Peterson and Ebuka Songs have mourned the death of their colleague, Toluwanisings. DAILY reports that Toluwanisings slumped at his Ibadan residence on Wednesday while about taking his children to school. According to his PA, Babadunni Gbolabo, the singer died after being rejected by seven hospitals in Ibadan, Oyo State. While tagging the incident as a big shock, Tope Alabi wrote, \u201cThis is such a big shock! I still can\u2019t wrap my head around this. It hurts, but I will not sorrow as those who have no hope. I find comfort in knowing that a saint has joined the angels.Recommended[\u2018Nigerians now have culture of begging\u2019 \u2013 Omotola Jalade](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/nigerians-now-have-culture-of-begging-omotola-jalade/)[I panicked after Davido stopped talking to me \u2013 Mayorkun](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/17/i-panicked-after-davido-stopped-talking-to-me-mayorkun/)[\u2018I defeated 17 Governors, won\u2019t support APC\u2019 \u2013 Davido](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/i-defeated-17-governors-wont-support-apc-davido/) \u201cToluwanisings, rest on, dear one, in the bosom of your Lord. May God comfort and strengthen your family, friends, and colleagues. You will forever be remembered.\u201d Yinka Alaseyori in a post on Instagram wrote, \u201cEven in our pain, Lord we judge you faithful. It is well. Rest Easy Soldier.\u201d Bidemi Olaoba posted on Instagram, \u201cLord, we judge You faithful, even in moments like this when words fail us and our hearts are heavy. Even when we do not understand, we choose to trust You. \u201cEven through the tears, we hold on to Your unfailing love. Lord, we still judge You faithful.\u201d Ebuka Songs wrote on his Instagram page, \u201cKo si kan kan ninu aye (there\u2019s nothing in this world). \u201cI Genuinely don\u2019t have words since the news of our beloved brother broke to me yesterday, but in all of it Lord we Judge you Faithful \u201cToday flight felt very different, became moment of deep reflection and truly all I can say is there\u2019s nothing in this world. Stay focused to your assignment. My Condolences to the families and friends of our dearest brother.\u201d Sharing a broken heart emoji alongside one of the deceased\u2019s songs, singer Peterson wrote, \u201cTOLUUUUUU0000000000UUUUU.\u201d Singer Busola Oke, better known as Eleyele, wrote on her page, \u201cWhy do good people leave so soon, Toluwanisings this is painful, your humility, talent, love for others and dedication to the kingdom\u2019s project is priceless. It is well Great Soldier, rest in power.\u201dShare this story[WhatsApp](https://wa.me/?text=Tope%20Alabi%2C%20Yinka%20Alaseyori%2C%20Bidemi%20Olaoba%2C%20Ebuka%20Songs%20mourn%20gospel%20singer%2C%20Toluwanisings%20https%3A%2F%2Fdailypost.ng%2F2026%2F10%2F16%2Ftope-alabi-yinka-alaseyori-bidemi-olaoba-ebuka-songs-mourn-gospel-singer-toluwanisings%2F) Facebook You may like[I\u2019ve never been an advocate for marriage \u2013 Uzor Arukwe](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/ive-never-been-an-advocate-for-marriage-uzor-arukwe/)[Nathaniel Bassey reacts to death of gospel singer, Toluwanisings](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/nathaniel-bassey-reacts-to-death-of-gospel-singer-toluwanisings/)[Gehgeh accuses VDM of threatening Davido over Burna Boy feud](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/gehgeh-accuses-vdm-of-threatening-davido-over-burna-boy-feud/)[Join the conversation](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/16/tope-alabi-yinka-alaseyori-bidemi-olaoba-ebuka-songs-mourn-gospel-singer-toluwanisings/comments/)", "content_hash": "95315c70a905e443a3c73e12765afc4f74669fce6524ae32a1ab57df6fdfe7f4", "domain": "dailypost", "fetched_at": "2026-10-18T04:30:23Z", "language": "en"}, {"id": "1024", "title": "Sunday, October 18, 2026", "url": "https://businessday.ng/todays-paper/", "final_url": "https://businessday.ng/todays-paper/", "text": "Today\u2019s Paper \u2013 Businessday NG bday: custom header code Marfeel bday: custom body-open code Sunday, October 18, 2026 Lagos --:-- London --:-- New York --:-- Dubai --:-- EN English (original) Arabic Chinese (Simplified) French German Hausa Igbo Portuguese (Brazil) Spanish Swahili Yoruba Menu [Today's Paper](https://businessday.ng/todays-paper/) Download App Tracking Trends | Informing Decisions [Subscribe Now](https://businessday.ng/subscribe/) [Sign In](https://businessday.ng/my-account) Welcome Log in or create a free account to get started. Welcome back, Saved Articles Read History [Go to My Account](https://businessday.ng/my-account) Log Out [Companies & Markets](https://businessday.ng/todays-paper/) [Companies](https://businessday.ng/category/companies/) [Markets](https://businessday.ng/category/markets/) [Economy](https://businessday.ng/category/business-economy/) [Agriculture](https://businessday.ng/category/agriculture/) [Aviation](https://businessday.ng/category/aviation/) [Banking](https://businessday.ng/category/banking/) [Maritime](https://businessday.ng/category/maritime/) [Real Estate](https://businessday.ng/category/real-estate/) [Transportation](https://businessday.ng/category/transport/) [Legal Business](https://businessday.ng/category/news/legal-business/) [Research post](https://businessday.ng/category/research-post/) [Investigation](https://businessday.ng/category/investigation/) [Hek](https://businessday.ng/category/newsletter/hek/) [Tax Calculator](https://businessday.ng/business-economy/article/tax-calculator/) [Tax360](https://businessday.ng/tag/tax360/